 the frames show:\n\n- **Frames 1 and 2**: A young girl (presumably Anne Frank) is holding a red-and-white checkered diary. She looks happy and is smiling. This is consistent with historical records that Anne received a diary for her 13th birthday (not her third), which is famously the start of her writing.\n  \n- **Frames 3–7**: A family scene in a dining room. A man (likely Otto Frank) is embracing Anne, who is still holding the diary. A woman (likely Edith Frank) sits at the table, and another woman stands nearby. The setting appears to be a birthday celebration, but again, the central gift is the diary.\n\n**Key observations:**\n\n- The gift clearly shown in the frames is a **diary**, not a doll.\n- There is **no doll visible** in any of the frames.\n- The context (Anne’s age, the diary, the family celebration) strongly suggests this is her **13th birthday**, not her third. Anne Frank was born in 1929; her third birthday would have been in 1932, long before the Nazi occupation and well before the events depicted in this video (which focus on 1942–1944).\n- The video’s narrative, as summarized, centers on Anne’s life during WWII and her diary — which began on her 13th birthday.\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nThe answer “2” (which corresponds to “A doll”) is **incorrect** based on the visual evidence in these frames. The first (and only) gift shown is a **diary**.\n\n✅ **Correct Answer: Not “A doll” — the gift shown is a diary.**'}], 'formatted_responses': ["\n=== Batch 0-30 (30 frames) ===\nFrames: /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/qAIRFyR6NyQ/frames/frame_0299.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/qAIRFyR6NyQ/frames/frame_0300.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/qAIRFyR6NyQ/frames/frame_0301.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/qAIRFyR6NyQ/frames/frame_0302.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/qAIRFyR6NyQ/frames/frame_0303.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/qAIRFyR6NyQ/frames/frame_0304.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed